# Product review page standard (template: Nike Vomero 18)

Reference implementation: `/reviews/nike-vomero-18` · seeds in `src/content/reviews-wave1.ts` (`review-vomero-18`).

When writing, rewriting, enriching, or auditing **any** product review, match this bar.

## 1. Voice

- Expert buying-guide editor — personal, specific, honest.
- Not a research paper, SEO listicle, hangtag listing, or “how to read this page” meta.
- Name peers, sessions, foams, widths, surfaces. Prefer “I'd shortlist / I'd pause / I'd rotate…”.
- Disclose once in testing context — never repeat “we didn’t test this” in every section.
- Detector: `src/lib/review/review-voice.ts` · agent: `agents/product-review/voice.md` · skill: `.cursor/skills/review-writer/SKILL.md`.

## 2. Buy if / Skip if

- **≥2–3 lines each**, full decision sentences (who + need + why this product / why not).
- Not telegram labels (“Trail runners”, “Tempo day athletes”).
- Name peers or fit constraints when useful.
- Glance “Best for” uses stacked bullets (shortened); comparison-table “Best for” stays punchy (`product.strengths[0]`).
- Enricher: `src/lib/review/audience-signals.ts` (page-time upgrade for thin signals).

## 3. Section depth

Every major shoe section (fit, cushioning, ride, stability, upper, grip, durability) needs real buyer insight — not one-line listings. Same bar for watches / racket / fitness with category criteria.

## 4. Section images

See `.cursor/rules/review-section-images.mdc`.

- **Required:** every major section on the page has its own product image when a hero exists.
- Product-only · one `src` per section · generate unique variants from the hero when missing · omit rather than duplicate or wrong brand.
- Path: `public/images/<sport>/products/<slug>/sections/<topic>.png` (`watches` for GPS/HRM)
- Resolver: `src/lib/review/resolve-section-visuals.ts`
- **Agent must generate missing section files before calling a review done.**

## 5. Internal linking

Plain review copy must link catalog mentions:

- Brand names → `/brands/<slug>`
- Other products → `/products/<slug>` (prefer page alternatives/peers for short aliases)

Use `LinkifiedText` / `segmentCatalogMentions` — do not leave bare “Brooks” / “Pegasus” in body copy when those entities exist in catalog.

## 6. Amazon / buy CTAs

Where an Amazon (or regional Amazon) offer exists, surface it in multiple places:

- Hero / score panel
- Mid-article strip
- Verdict card (primary)
- Where-to-buy list (“View on Amazon”)
- Footer under offers

Helpers: `src/lib/review/amazon-offer.ts`, `ReviewAmazonCta`. Affiliate disclosure stays near offers. Never invent prices in prose.

## 7. Scores / gauges

Metric “why” blurbs are product-specific — not “Excellent for this product’s intended role” templates (`metric-editorials.ts`).

## Definition of done (any review)

- [ ] Clear bottom line / verdict for a real use case
- [ ] Buy if / Skip if detailed (≥2–3 each)
- [ ] No `isReportOrJunkVoice` on enriched bodies
- [ ] Unique product section images for every major section — generated from hero if missing; no hero stamp; no other brands
- [ ] Brand/product mentions link internally
- [ ] Amazon/buy CTAs present when offers exist
- [ ] Would still make sense read aloud to a friend in a shop
